# --- Formats this repository deliberately does not hand to Prettier ---------------------------
#
# `npm run format:check` is `prettier --check .` as of issue #1660. It was an allowlist of
# eighty-one hand-written paths, so a new file was unformatted until somebody remembered it. The
# exclusions below are the whole of what Prettier does not see, and each one states why.
#
# Markdown: markdownlint-cli2 gates it (`npm run lint:md`, a required CI step), and the two
# disagree by design — `markdownlint-sentences-per-line` splits prose one sentence per line while
# Prettier's `proseWrap` default is `preserve`. Two formatters over one corpus is a standing
# conflict, so markdown has exactly one owner and it is not Prettier.
*.md

# Workflow YAML is read as SOURCE TEXT by `tests/ci-workflow-semantics.test.js` and
# `tests/helpers/workflow-source.js`, and `pr-screenshots.yml` carries a step name asserted from
# two other places. Reformatting is measurable risk for no gain.
.github/

# The canonical spec source of truth (AGENTS.md). Reformatting it churns the exact diff that
# post-implementation and docs reviewers reconcile against each issue's change delta.
openspec/

# Jekyll owns the docs site; its build output and vendored assets are already excluded above.
docs/

# Machine-written and rewritten by `npm run benchmark:performance`. Formatting it here would be
# undone by the next run, so the two would disagree forever.
benchmarks/baselines/

# The compiled stylesheet. Its source of truth is the component `<style>` blocks and the design
# tokens; stylelint gates those.
styles/fabricate.css

